.TH TENSOR-MINERU-ADAPTER 1 "November 2026" "Tensor GPU source-only adapter" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensor-mineru-adapter.py \- stage and reconcile per-PDF MinerU work using the existing GPU queue
.SH DESCRIPTION
This Python module is a library, not a standalone service. PDFAdapter stages
regular PDF bytes in a private queue-adjacent directory and submits distinct
mineru_pdf records keyed by conversion revision and SHA-256 digest. run_one
claims one record under the existing queue worker lock and a caller-supplied
GPU admission context, then invokes a caller-supplied conversion callback.
The callback must use the installed MinerU conversion backend and return a
real output_root/gradio/<run> directory containing middle_json.json,
markdown.md, and structured_content.json. Artifact names were verified
against the installed MinerU RunArtifacts implementation.
.SH RECOVERY
Before conversion, a private manifest records that dispatch may occur. A
successful callback records the output location and SHA-256 digests of the
three retained artifacts before queue completion. Failed or expired PDF
attempts are never retried automatically, because the native POST may already
have succeeded. reconcile(job_id) can complete a failed job only if its
manifest records a completed result and every retained artifact still exists
with the recorded digest. Missing task/result evidence requires manual native
reconciliation, not re-dispatch.
.SH SECURITY
The adapter refuses symlink and non-regular inputs, non-PDF headers, empty
files, and files above 128 MiB. The staging root must be a private mode-0700
folder. The callback must keep its GPU admission context until the GPU model
has actually released memory, including failure cleanup. Do not enable this
adapter without shared request admission and a verified MinerU hook.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Source-only. No deployed conversion-service hook or GPU admission context is
provided. The adapter itself cannot discover the dynamic MinerU router port,
prevent a second WebUI user from converting outside the queue, or persist a
native task ID if the MinerU POST succeeds but the client loses its response.
In that ambiguous case, preserve the failed record and inspect native state.
.SH SEE ALSO
